# THE 300 s WINDOW IS NOT SOURCE. `window-300s-16k.wav` is one caged ffmpeg
# command from the frozen corpus (docs/live-concurrency-budget.md §"What is being
# run", with the pinned sha256 f351295b9770685c37cdddf29071937afe155b4e16f52f123d8f00084f3bab90):
#
#   ffmpeg -i _main/bench/discord-call-20261116/mix-16k.wav -ss 360 -t 300 \
#          -ac 1 -ar 16000 -c:a pcm_s16le -y _main/bench/concurrency/window-300s-16k.wav
#
# so a rebuilt window compares byte for byte without 9.6 MB of audio living in the
# index. The receipts that DO live here are the numbers: n1..n5.json and logs-n*/,
# which is what the doc's table is derived from.
*.wav
*.opus

__pycache__/
